    "wholeTokenBoundary": "Every Latin run is one complete registered token; no normalization, numeric-tone spellings, combining marks, per-letter fallback, unknown syllables or synthesized wrong combinations.",
    "componentBoundary": "p/b/d/l/n/x/q/j are support call names for visible P5-P7 components; y is only for P8/P9 static-form description. They do not authorize initial-plus-final audio assembly or claim short-consonant performance. Written iě/ié/iē/üè/ué/uē remain visual components, not independent audio targets.",
    "toneBoundary": "ie and ye use ye1; üe and yue use yue1; er uses er1 as explicitly requested base demonstration. Only printed actual syllable tones are added, never full four-tone rows. 儿 is an inert carrier for er1; its lexical er2 reading is separately encoded for ér.",
    "umlautBoundary": "lüè/nüè propose lve4/nve4, extending the same v spelling convention as registered nv3/lv2; provider acceptance and audible results for these new strings have not been observed. jué/quē/xué use complete jue2/que1/xue2, never jv/qv/xv fallback.",
    "naturalChineseWords": "Ordinary Chinese remains natural speech; 梅花开/雪花飘/夜色美 are not whole-word overrides. Their printed pinyin tokens are separately whitelisted. No unknown Chinese-word phoneme override is guessed.",
